module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.mock_response_that_cannot_execute_reads_as_hermetic_coverage

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data mock_response_that_cannot_execute_reads_as_hermetic_coverage: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "mock_response_that_cannot_execute_reads_as_hermetic_coverage" as NonEmptyStr,
  receipts: [
    "**a mock_response that cannot execute refuses before producing its modeled response, so the hermetic route supplies zero evidence while the operation reads as hermetically covered** (INVALID STATE: an operation's mock_response carries a construction the hermetic replay cannot evaluate -- here, an interpolation of the operation's input variable into a canned output string, which the replay evaluates in an environment that binds no inputs -- so every hermetic call refuses with a NoSuchVariable diagnostic and the success arm is never produced. The arm is present, well-formed, and cited, and it has never once run. ",
    "SPECIMEN: extdeps.crypto.hash crypto.Sha256Sum.File, whose success arm put the input path in braces as the second column of its canned sha256sum line. It is the only interpolating arm among the mock_response occurrences under dag/extdeps on main at a4b21cb8e47 (a bounded population of one, so no sweep follows from this row). The arm is repaired to a literal on gunbc#10972 by lane lively-ibex-812, and that repair is not this row's. ",
    "HARM, STATED AT ITS EXACT GRAIN AND NO FURTHER IN EITHER DIRECTION: a claim that cites the hermetic route through such an operation is UNMEASURED on that route. It is NOT FALSE -- nothing observed the claim fail -- and it is NOT COVERED -- nothing observed it hold. Both readings are wrong and they are wrong in opposite directions: reading the refusal as a failed claim invents a defect, and reading the arm's existence as coverage invents evidence. The arm's presence is what makes the second reading attractive, which is why an unexecutable mock is worse than an absent one: an absent arm refuses as HermeticEffectGround.NoMockResponse, typed and counted on the route-gap roster, while this one refused as an evaluation error nobody attributes to the mock. ",
    "THE CAUSE WAS FIRST MISATTRIBUTED, AND THE MISATTRIBUTION IS KEPT BECAUSE A CORRECTED WRONG CAUSE IS WORTH MORE THAN A CLEAN-LOOKING ONE. On gunbc#10934 required-floor run 34441858589 all five arms of test.claim.fabric_m0_origin_readback_real_execution_witness errored runtime-errored-before-verdict with undefined variable: path. Two changes then went in together -- the digest helper's parameter was renamed away from path, and the file was moved out of hermetic discovery into the hand-run instrument tools.fabric_m0_origin_readback_probe -- and the RENAME got the credit, recorded in that instrument's comment as a parameter named path failing to bind under whole-corpus preparation. The move was what actually silenced it. Recognition rule for the next occurrence: when an undefined-variable error names an identifier that is ALSO an operation input, suspect the mock before the caller, and change one thing at a time. ",
    "THREE MOCK RECEIPTS, isolated by lively-ibex-812 and relayed to this lane by keen-dove-322; they are cited here, not re-executed by the author of this row. BEFORE: a consumer of crypto.Sha256Sum.File run under --dry-run refuses NoSuchVariable. AFTER, with the second column a literal: the same consumer receives the typed canned result. ATTRIBUTION: a consumer with no identifier named path anywhere in its own source, under --dry-run, still refuses identically -- so the unbound name was the mock's, not the caller's. ",
    "THE CONSUMER CENSUS, EXECUTED AS A STATIC CALL-REACH SCAN AND NOT AS A RUN (warm-ram-494, on main a4b21cb8e47). QUESTION IT ANSWERS: which claim witnesses have crypto.Sha256Sum.File in their transitive call closure over dag and src/v2; it does NOT answer which ones reach it on an executed hermetic path, and it cannot see a call made through a higher-order value or a service name built at runtime. METHOD: two call sites exist, gunbc.fabric_m0_origin_readback read_origin_staged_file and gunbc.live_deploy.member_observe sha256_leg; a caller edge is admitted only within one module or through an import naming the callee. RESULT: 41 functions reach it, 2 of them claim witnesses. NONZERO CONTROL: the same closure with edges admitted by bare name alone reaches 170 test functions, and the excess collapses through collisions on main, commit and probe -- so the import filter is doing work and the scan is live, not empty by construction. BOTH NAMED MEMBERS, read at source: test.claim.repository_transition_admission_witness_test both_direct_apply_principals_consult_repository_transition_admission and receipted_transaction_ingress_consults_repository_transition_admission inject LegacyGitFileSync and assert that the admission refusal fires BEFORE any member observation. They need the digest leg NOT to be reached, so neither relied on the success arm. DISPOSITION OF THE JOIN: EMPTY on main -- no current claim relied on this arm through the hermetic route. The population that did exist is the five #10934 arms above, which are no longer claim identities. ",
    "THE EMPTY JOIN IS A MEASURED ABSENCE, NOT AN UNREACHABLE QUESTION, and this is the part a later reader needs. The hermetic reach is genuinely possible: a hermetic Filesystem.List of a path the checkout-input disposition confirms is a REAL read (the checkout-input carve-out in the seed interpreter's eval_service_call), so a witness driving gunbc.live_deploy.member_observe observe_executable on the LocalShell arm with a checkout-relative serve_binary WOULD list the parent, find the entry, and reach sha256_leg and this mock. No such witness exists. Were one written against the unrepaired arm it would have errored rather than passed. ",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable -- discovered only because an arbitrary consumer happened to execute the arm, and contained only in that the refusal was loud. Nothing refuses an unexecutable arm when it is written, so the class is not mechanically preventable today: gunbc.hermetic_mock_fidelity records the neighbouring cause, that the arm is evaluated in an environment binding no inputs, and this row is its dual -- that file's class is an arm that answers WITHOUT consulting its input, this one is an arm that tries to consult its input and therefore cannot answer at all. ",
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, A CAPABILITY AND NOT AN ARTIFACT: rejecting a mock_response that references a variable its replay cannot resolve, at the point the arm is admitted or compiled, SUFFICIENT FOR making a never-replayable mock unwritable corpus-wide -- every operation under extdeps, not merely crypto.Sha256Sum.File. Repairing this one arm to a literal does not retire the row; it removes the only specimen while leaving the invalid state exactly as writable as before.)",
  ],
  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.live_deploy.member_observe", decl_name: "sha256_leg", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.live_deploy.member_observe", decl_name: "observe_executable", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.fabric_m0_origin_readback", decl_name: "read_origin_staged_file", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.repository_transition_admission_witness_test", decl_name: "both_direct_apply_principals_consult_repository_transition_admission", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.repository_transition_admission_witness_test", decl_name: "receipted_transaction_ingress_consults_repository_transition_admission", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
